# Archfile — the Arch counterpart to Brewfile.
#
# Same idea, same vocabulary: one package per line, prefixed by where it comes from.
#   pac    official repos (pacman)
#   aur    AUR (yay)
#   npm    global npm package
#   cargo  cargo install
# Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored. Read by bootstrap.sh on Linux.
#
# Every Brewfile entry is accounted for below — either ported, or listed under
# "Deliberately not ported" at the bottom with the reason. If you add something to
# the Brewfile, the honest thing is to decide its fate here in the same commit.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Compositor and desktop shell   (macOS: aerospace, sketchybar, borders, raycast)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
pac hyprland                  # <- aerospace
pac waybar                    # <- sketchybar
pac hyprlock
pac hypridle
pac hyprpaper
pac hyprpicker                # colour picker
pac hyprpolkitagent           # GUI auth prompts; without it sudo-GUI actions hang
pac rofi-wayland              # <- raycast. NOT plain `rofi` — that one is X11-only.
pac mako                      # notifications (macOS had none to port; it just had NC)
pac wl-clipboard
pac cliphist                  # <- raycast clipboard history
pac grim
pac slurp
pac brightnessctl
pac playerctl                 # <- plugins/wnp-daemon/media_daemon.py, but built in
pac qt5-wayland
pac qt6-wayland
pac xdg-desktop-portal-hyprland
pac xdg-desktop-portal-gtk    # file pickers for GTK apps; not optional in practice
pac polkit
aur swayosd                   # macOS-style volume/brightness OSD overlay
aur wlogout                   # power menu
aur rofi-emoji                # SUPER+. picker
aur rofi-calc

# `borders` has no port and needs none — Hyprland draws window borders itself, and
# hyprland.lua already carries the 0x88ffffff / 0x20ffffff colours it was configured
# with. Same for `swipeaerospace`: hl.gesture() is native.

